  "text": "Keyboard and picture controls\n\nGo to see someone or a place.\n\ntranslate(188 144) scale(.22)\n\nSee the ending you are trying\n\nI want to bring the seed back\n\nNotice sounds with your ears.\n\nOnto the land from the water.\n\nBefore another event happens.\n\nis expecting a different time\n\nM0-105q-23 18 0 45 22-26 0-45\n\nNot thought likely to happen.\n\ngarden-status garden-feedback\n\nTake Grandma’s story to Mara.\n\nThink about a later gathering\n\nA narrow split in a surface.\n\nBring out Grandma’s cushions\n\nGrandma has Mara’s page now.\n\nM146 117q19-7 35-1l3 20h-39Z\n\nRead these moments with help\n\nSee how your plan would work\n\nTell Grandma what Mara said.\n\nOn the subject of something.\n\nboy’s promise to his sister.\n\nAn illustration of the story\n\nMade accessible or unfolded.\n\ngarden-app g-adaptive-reader\n\nShort for she is or she has.\n\nAt or to a greater distance.\n\nAllowed something to happen.\n\ng-choices g-adaptive-choices\n\nOne more or a different one.\n\nSol: has not heard the time.\n\nHaving lived for more years.\n\nTo one side, out of the way.\n\nBack to Mara’s earlier story\n\nThe ending you helped create\n\nLet Mara cross to the garden\n\nWhat turns flour into dough?\n\nGrandma is holding the seed.\n\nMore than one loaf of bread.\n\nPlaces where people can sit.\n\nOne piece of a larger whole.\n\nReread the time you told Sol\n\nHanded something to someone.\n\nWanting something to happen.\n\nThe Empty Bench · by Grandma\n\nAdditional people or things.\n\ngift they repaired together.\n\nAn ending from Sol’s account\n\nLifted to a higher position.\n\nKept something in the hands.\n\nConnect to the first section\n\nWatching Loop’s picture show\n\nRead this conversation aloud\n\nWhy not just move the flour?\n\nLikely to happen or be true.\n\nHappening or being used now.\n\nSparkFest and Loop’s welcome\n\nMake something ready to use.",
